Design System Toolkit — skills/lisa-brand/, references/brand-extraction.md,
                        assets/lisa-brand-book-a4.html
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The brand-extraction procedure — extract from the reference before asking,
never invent a brand detail, never redraw a logo, finish the job by rendering
the PDF — and the single-A4 brand-book form with its print trio (`@page` A4
at zero margin, exact print colours, a fixed-millimetre page) are derived
from RoboNuggets' Design System Toolkit skill.

  Upstream:  https://github.com/robonuggets/design-system
  Author:    RoboNuggets
  License:   MIT
  Changes:   Derived, not copied. Rewritten as a Hi Ted, Meet Lisa skill:
             the output is a design.md on the templates' shared token schema
             with per-token provenance (fact / approx), consumed by /lisa
             through the intake's style answer; the A4 skeleton is rebuilt
             brand-neutral with LISA:CONTENT fences, bracketed slots and the
             house colophon; the scrollable design-system.html page is not
             carried. Added: a contrast check on the extracted colour pairs
             (reported, never repainted), a fonts-ready wait and an
             embedded-font assertion before the PDF counts as rendered,
             overflow: visible on the page plus a page-count assertion, and
             sanitisation of any SVG lifted from a web page (scripts,
             handlers, foreignObject and external hrefs stripped).

